= Mechanism design — Technical =

A direct mechanism can be represented by an outcome rule g(θ̂) applied to reported types θ̂. A dominant-strategy incentive-compatible mechanism satisfies <pre>u_i(g(θ_i,θ_-i),θ_i) ≥ u_i(g(θ̂_i,θ_-i),θ_i)</pre>for every i, true type θ_i, alternative report θ̂_i, and others' reports θ_-i.

== Modeling cautions ==
* mechanism design ≠ generic product design
* mechanism design ≠ assuming truthful behavior
* incentive compatibility ≠ fairness or optimality on every criterion

== References ==
* The Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences, 2007 Prize in Economic Sciences materials on mechanism design theory.
* Leonid Hurwicz, Eric Maskin & Roger Myerson, foundational mechanism-design and implementation literature.
* Roger B. Myerson, “Optimal Auction Design” (1981).
